  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>The Tikayan Le Méditerranée campsite sits at the tip of the Giens peninsula, in Hyères, 150 m from La Badine beach according to the official website. It offers only mobile homes for rent (101, for 2 to 8 people, air-conditioned) and no pitches for tents, caravans or motorhomes. On site: a restaurant-bar "Le Mojito", a pizzeria, a grocery, a playground and two petanque courts; bus line 67 (Badine stop) goes to the centre of Hyères.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you book</h2>
      <p>The official website's FAQ answers: "Yes, dogs under 40 kg are accepted in most of our rentals". The rental pages show a "Dog under 40 kg allowed" pictogram: some rentals do not have it, so check the page of the accommodation you choose.</p>
      <p>Specialist directories add: up-to-date vaccination record, dog on a lead in the campsite, 2 pets maximum, categories 1 and 2 refused. For the supplement, a tour operator writes €5 per day and per animal, a specialist directory €3 to €6 per day depending on the period; the official website read gives no amount. A €300 deposit appears on a tour operator's page.</p>
      <p><strong>To check before you go:</strong> the amount of the supplement, the two-dog limit and whether dogs are accepted in the campsite's restaurant (stated by a directory, not found on the official website), by contacting the campsite before booking.</p>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The La Badine beach restaurants can be reached on foot from the campsite according to the official website (dog rules of these restaurants not checked).</p>

      <h2>Sources</h2>
      <p>Official website tikayan.com (campsite page and FAQ), specialist dog travel directories (Tourisme avec mon chien, EmmeneTonChien) and tour operator pages for the detailed conditions, read on 08/11/2026.</p>
